### Initialize Moose Project

Source: https://github.com/514-labs/moosestack/blob/main/apps/framework-docs-v2/content/guides/static-report-generation.mdx

Create a new Moose project using the typescript-empty template and install dependencies.

```bash
moose init sales-reports typescript-empty
cd sales-reports
pnpm install
```

--------------------------------

### Define ClickHouse Event Model in TypeScript

Source: https://github.com/514-labs/moosestack/blob/main/apps/framework-docs-v2/content/moosestack/getting-started/existing-app/fastify.mdx

Define a TypeScript interface for your ClickHouse table schema and create an OlapTable instance. Moose will automatically create this table when 'moose dev' is run.

```typescript
import { OlapTable } from "@514labs/moose-lib";

export interface EventModel {
  id: string;
  amount: number;
  event_time: Date;
  status: 'completed' | 'active' | 'inactive';
}

export const Events = new OlapTable<EventModel>("events", {
  orderByFields: ["event_time"],
});
```

--------------------------------

### Define OLAP Table and Materialized View in TypeScript

Source: https://github.com/514-labs/moosestack/blob/main/apps/framework-docs-v2/content/moosestack/index.mdx

Use the OlapTable class to define a table schema and MaterializedView to create aggregated views for analytics. This is useful for setting up data warehousing and analytical queries.

```typescript
const table = new OlapTable<Event>("events");

const mv = new MaterializedView<AggregatedEvent>({
  selectStatement: sql.statement`
    SELECT count(*) as count, name
    FROM ${table}
    GROUP BY name
  `,
  selectTables: [table],
  tableName: "events",
  materializedViewName: "aggregated_events"
});
```

--------------------------------

### Api Query Endpoint

Source: https://github.com/514-labs/moosestack/blob/main/apps/framework-docs-v2/content/moosestack/reference/index.mdx

Creates an HTTP endpoint for querying data with request and response types.

```typescript
// Basic usage
export const myApi = new Api<UserQuery, UserProfile[]>(
  "getUserProfiles",
  async (params, { client, sql }) => {
    const result = await client.query.execute(
      sql.statement`SELECT * FROM user_profiles WHERE age > ${params.minAge} LIMIT 10`
    );
    return result;
  }
);
```

```python
# Basic usage
def get_user_profiles(params: UserQuery) -> list[UserProfile]:
    # Query implementation
    return [UserProfile(...), UserProfile(...)]

my_api = Api[UserQuery, list[UserProfile]](
    "get_user_profiles",
    get_user_profiles
)
```

--------------------------------

### Create Multi-Database ClickHouse View in TypeScript

Source: https://github.com/514-labs/moosestack/blob/main/apps/framework-docs-v2/content/moosestack/olap/model-view.mdx

Pass a `database` argument to the `View` constructor to create the view in a specific ClickHouse database. Moose will qualify the view name as `` `database`.`view_name` ``.

```typescript
import { View, sql } from "@514labs/moose-lib";
import { events } from "./Events";

export const rawEvents = new View(
  "raw_events",
  sql.statement`SELECT * FROM ${events}`,
  [events],
  { database: "analytics" },
);

```

